\textbf{Abstract:} Traditionally, Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) has been utilized to extract latent topics from text documents. Nevertheless, these topics often lack precision, being either too general or too specific. To resolve this, we propose a novel topic model capable of generating granular topics. Our approach employs a hierarchical structure in which a coarse topic is decomposed into several finer topics. We show that the model successfully produces granular topics of varying widths and achieves topically coherent representations superior to LDA. Additionally, our results indicate that the model generates more diverse topics than LDA and achieves better NMI scores. Finally, we demonstrate the model's ability to produce finely grained topics from medical literature.
